## Joining name arenas, for the `.tbd` decode on workers (speed-sol2-link-inputs, 2026-10-30)

What is slow: `macho/tbd.rs` now parses a stream's documents in parallel (A6), but decodes them into the one `Names` arena of the `Shared` serially: about 0.5 ms of libSystem.tbd's 0.8 ms (see `docs/v2/plan/lanes/link/speed-of-light.md`, Mach-O, "Parse `.tbd`"). Each document could decode into its own `Names` on a worker if the reader could join them afterwards, which it can't: `Name`'s fields are private to `model.rs`.

The exact edit, in `model.rs` after `Names::bytes`:

```rust
    /// Appends `other`'s names, returning the offset its names start at here: a [`Name`] of
    /// `other` is [`Name::shifted`] by it to name the same text in `self`. An error past 4 GiB.
    pub fn append(&mut self, other: &Names) -> Result<u32, String> {
        let at = u32::try_from(self.0.len()).ok();
        let len = u32::try_from(other.0.len()).ok();
        match (at, len) {
            (Some(at), Some(len)) if at.checked_add(len).is_some() => {
                self.0.push_str(&other.0);
                Ok(at)
            }
            // alloc: error path
            _ => Err("more than 4 GiB of names in one file".to_owned()),
        }
    }
```

and on `Name`:

```rust
impl Name {
    /// The same name in the arena `by` came from: `by` must be what [`Names::append`] returned
    /// for the arena this name was made in.
    pub fn shifted(self, by: u32) -> Name {
        Name { at: self.at + by, len: self.len }
    }
}
```

Character boundaries are kept: `other` is a whole `String` appended, so every boundary of it is one in `self`. Nothing else changes; the core still checks every name of a file when it takes it.

My side once it is in: `tbd.rs` `decode` per document on workers (`map_init` with a `Names` and a `Seen` each), then a serial join of the documents in order that appends each arena once, shifts its symbols' names, and deduplicates across documents with the one `Seen` it keeps today (only names seen in an earlier document are dropped, as now). Test: a differential against the serial decode on the seeded streams of `documents_parse_alike_on_workers_and_in_turn`.

Related, already filed, the core's: 00004 (`Shared::index`, so `Exports` hashes only imported names; `tbd.rs`'s `Seen` is that table).
